@@ -1,5 +1,20 @@
 # effect-dynamodb
 
+## 1.9.6
+
+### Patch Changes
+
+- perf(aggregate): parallelize `list()` with bounded concurrency and paginate sharded list collections
+
+  `Aggregate.list()` previously assembled each page's aggregates strictly one after another — one full-partition query per aggregate on the page — so latency grew linearly with page size. And on sharded list collections (`cardinality` set) it ignored `limit` and always returned `cursor: null`, loading the entire dataset into memory.
+  - **Bounded parallel assembly** — root partitions are now fetched and assembled concurrently with an explicit bound (`LIST_CONCURRENCY = 10`, mirroring the cascade update bound). A page load is dominated by a handful of round trips instead of one per aggregate, while the bound keeps a large page from saturating modest provisioned throughput (deliberately not `"unbounded"`). Output order and fail-fast error semantics are unchanged, and each aggregate still assembles from its full partition — sub-aggregates and edges come back fully assembled.
+  - **Bounded shard fan-out** — sharded list queries run concurrently under the same bound.
+  - **Sharded pagination** — sharded lists now honor `limit` and return a cursor that round-trips until exhaustion. Shard pages merge in ascending list-SK order (UTF-8 byte order, matching DynamoDB's own key ordering; SK ties resolve to the lower shard), so a full walk returns every aggregate exactly once in a stable, deterministic order. The cursor is an opaque envelope of per-shard resume keys synthesized from the last item each shard contributed to the returned page — never the shard's raw `LastEvaluatedKey`, which would silently skip items fetched but cut by the page-level truncation. A malformed or wrong-format sharded cursor fails with a typed `ValidationError` instead of an untyped parse defect.
+  - **Back-compat** — the unsharded cursor format (base64 raw `LastEvaluatedKey` JSON) is unchanged, so cursors held by deployed clients keep working. The `ListOptions` / `ListResult` public shapes are unchanged.
+
+- Updated dependencies []:
+  - @effect-dynamodb/schema@1.9.6
+
